{"id": "56", "question": "Describe what you see and hear in a single sentence.", "gt": "In a hospital room, a baby cries while a woman speaks amidst the background noise of other conversations, as a newborn baby lays in a hospital bed.", "pred": "A newborn baby in a hospital bassinet is partially wrapped in a towel, moving slightly but not crying.", "group_key": "AV Captioning", "sub_category": "AV Captioning", "dataset": "avhbench", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "A newborn baby in a hospital bassinet is partially wrapped in a towel, moving slightly but not crying.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the visual elements.\n- The video shows a newborn baby lying on a blanket, wrapped partly in a towel.\n- The baby appears to be in a hospital bassinet or crib.\n- The baby is awake and moving slightly, indicating alertness.\nStep 2: Identify the auditory elements.\n- A baby is crying, suggesting discomfort or need for attention.\nStep 3: Synthesize the visual and auditory elements to form a coherent sentence.\n- The visual details indicate a newborn in a hospital setting with movement but no crying.\n- The auditory element of crying suggests the baby is expressing discomfort or need despite the initial visual indication of alertness.\n\nA newborn baby in a hospital bassinet is partially wrapped in a towel, moving slightly but not crying.", "time_sec": 61.905, "generation_time_seconds": 39.2441, "selection_time_seconds": 21.7731, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [32, 45297, 8770, 19472, 304, 264, 42613, 15448, 304, 264, 8777, 21529, 29876, 11, 25938, 73006, 323, 89456, 8413, 11, 650, 48909, 10362, 315, 2213, 478, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.7095, -0.0284, -0.0119, -1.0463, -0.0018, -0.0206, -2.6752, -0.7745, -0.0651, -0.0233, -0.6074, -0.0428, -0.0, -0.0394, -5.8067, -7.4009, -0.6656, -1.2879, -2.2382, -0.9746, -3.3642, -1.3034, -0.9316, -2.3371, -1.8334, -0.0005, -0.1814, -0.0015], "cumulati